    "reference": "A concrete slab can be either \"ground-bearing\" or \"suspended.\" A slab is \"ground-bearing\" if it rests directly on the foundation, while a \"suspended\" slab does not. Suspended slabs are commonly used in double-storey or multi-storey buildings."
